adjudication.rationale:
The new API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts` authenticates solely via:
```ts
if (req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !== process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET)
  return 403;
```
If `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` is truly unset (i.e., `undefined`) and the request omits that header (so the header lookup is also `undefined`), the comparison becomes `undefined !== undefined` which is `false`, so the request is accepted (fail-open). After that, `userId` and `appSlug` come directly from the parsed body and are used to `update`/`create` credentials for that user without any other authz checks, so bypassing the secret check enables overwriting/creating credentials for arbitrary users/apps. This behavior is directly present in the diff; reachability still depends on `APP_CREDENTIAL_SHARING_ENABLED`, but the missing fail-closed guard when the secret is absent is real.
